@exit/1
#exit/1
exit(N) terminates the Prolog system. N must be an integer.
This number is the return value of the whole Prolog system.
(the argument of the C function exit() that ends Prolog)
@halt/0
@end/0
#ensure/3
HU-Prolog implements a simple library concept.
ensure(Lib, Name, Arity) loads the predicate `Name/Arity' from
the library `Lib'. The following rules apply:
- If the predicate is already defined or has already been
  successfully(!) loaded from a library once, ensure/3
  succeeds without further action.
- If the predicate is not contained in the library,
  ensure/3 fails.
- In every other case the predicate is loaded from the
  library.

Undefined predicates can be loaded automatically with
unknown/1.

In the current implementation, predicates loaded with ensure
are not shown by listing/0. That may change again.
@Library Structure
@unknown/1
@listing/0
#Library Structure
A library currently consists of a directory in the file system
of the operating system. Under UNIX a call of the form
    ensure('/usr/local/lib/huprolog/',member,1)
causes the file '/usr/local/lib/huprolog/member.1' to be
taken as the definition of the predicate member/1. This file
is loaded with consult/1 when needed. It is only a
convention, not a requirement, that this file actually
contains the corresponding predicate.
#eof/0
eof is true if the end of file of the current input stream
has been reached.
